<title>RUSSIA: Russian GDP rises 0.2 pct yr/yr in Q1 1997.</title>
<headline>Russian GDP rises 0.2 pct yr/yr in Q1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian gross domestic product in the first quarter of this year totalled 605 trillion roubles, 0.2 percent higher than a year earlier in inflation-adjusted terms, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>GDP in March was 0.3 percent lower than a year earlier.</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN GDP			   Q1 97     Q4 96     Q1 96</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change	    +0.2	N/A	 -3</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN GDP			  MAR 97    FEB 97    MAR 97</p>
<p>    month-on-month pct change	  +2	  -2	  +3</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change	    -0.3	+0.9	-4</p>
<p>Note - Official Russian data tend to underreport a growing private sector in the economy.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
